{"uid":"91afde35b488b5a1","name":"test_waive_toggle_round_trip_preserves_a_single_trailing_newline[newline-only]","fullName":"tests.test_hub_parked_actions#test_waive_toggle_round_trip_preserves_a_single_trailing_newline","historyId":"9f5e15e26f569add3e0f3c5f4058e325","time":{"start":1792071941959,"stop":1792071941959,"duration":0},"description":"cure-01-01-5 (B.3-B.5): the companion bug to the unterminated-line\n    fix above -- operator prose that ALREADY ends in exactly one real\n    newline is byte-identical to what `applyWaiveLine` produces right\n    after inserting its own separator for UNTERMINATED prose, so a naive\n    fix that always strips a lone trailing newline on uncheck instead\n    silently eats the operator's own byte. The review's own probe found\n    exactly this: checking then unchecking F1 turned \"operator note\n\"\n    into \"operator note\" with zero requests. Exercised with multiple\n    toggles (check, uncheck, check, uncheck again) since a stateful fix\n    could get the FIRST round trip right and a later one wrong.","descriptionHtml":"<p>cure-01-01-5 (B.3-B.5): the companion bug to the unterminated-line<br />\nfix above -- operator prose that ALREADY ends in exactly one real<br />\nnewline is byte-identical to what <code>applyWaiveLine</code> produces right<br />\nafter inserting its own separator for UNTERMINATED prose, so a naive<br />\nfix that always strips a lone trailing newline on uncheck instead<br />\nsilently eats the operator's own byte. The review's own probe found<br />\nexactly this: checking then unchecking F1 turned &quot;operator note<br />\n&quot;<br />\ninto &quot;operator note&quot; with zero requests. Exercised with multiple<br />\ntoggles (check, uncheck, check, uncheck again) since a stateful fix<br />\ncould get the FIRST round trip right and a later one wrong.</p>\n","status":"skipped","statusMessage":"Skipped: node not installed","statusTrace":"('/__w/ralphd/ralphd/tests/test_hub_parked_actions.py', 302, 'Skippe